---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["Is BIMI free?", "The DNS record is free, but Gmail requires a VMC certificate ($1,000-1,500/year) to display the logo. Apple Mail may work without a VMC in some cases."], ["What logo format does BIMI require?", "SVG Tiny 1.2 (a specific SVG profile). The logo must be square, fit within specific dimensions, and have no external references."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "BIMI Record",
  description: "BIMI record: display your brand logo in Gmail and Apple Mail. Requires DMARC enforcement and a VMC certificate.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "BIMI Record" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="BIMI Record: Display Your Brand Logo in Email Inboxes (DMARC Required)"
  description="BIMI record: display your brand logo in Gmail and Apple Mail. Requires DMARC enforcement and a VMC certificate."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">BIMI Record</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">BIMI Record</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-dim">BIMI record: display your brand logo in Gmail and Apple Mail inboxes. Requires DMARC enforcement and VMC.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Requirement</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>DMARC enforcement</td><td>p=quarantine or p=reject (p=none is not sufficient)</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>DNS record</td><td>TXT at default._bimi.domain.com: v=BIMI1; l=https://url/to/logo.svg</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>Logo format</td><td>SVG Tiny 1.2 profile (specific requirements apply)</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>VMC certificate</td><td>Verified Mark Certificate from DigiCert or Entrust (required for Gmail)</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>Supported providers</td><td>Gmail, Apple Mail (iOS 16+), Yahoo Mail, Fastmail</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>A BIMI (Brand Indicators for Message Identification) record is a DNS TXT record published at default._bimi.domain.com that specifies the location of a brand logo to be displayed next to verified email messages in supporting inbox providers.</p><p class='mt-3'>BIMI requires DMARC enforcement at p=quarantine or p=reject as a prerequisite, ensuring that only authenticated email from the domain displays the brand logo.</p><p class='mt-3'>Gmail additionally requires a Verified Mark Certificate (VMC) issued by a trusted certificate authority to validate the trademark ownership of the logo before displaying it.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">BIMI is a post-DMARC feature: do not attempt it until DMARC enforcement is at p=quarantine or p=reject. The VMC certificate costs $1,000-1,500 per year, which is a significant investment for the logo display benefit.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is BIMI free?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The DNS record is free, but Gmail requires a VMC certificate ($1,000-1,500/year) to display the logo. Apple Mail may work without a VMC in some cases.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What logo format does BIMI require?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">SVG Tiny 1.2 (a specific SVG profile). The logo must be square, fit within specific dimensions, and have no external references.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
